{
    "background_story": "Collins was a skilled craftsman with a passion for woodworking. Growing up in a family of carpenters, he learned the art of joinery from a young age. After completing his apprenticeship, Collins set out to make a name for himself in the world of fine furniture making. He became known for his exceptional attention to detail and ability to bring together seemingly disparate pieces of wood into beautiful, functional works of art. Collins' love for joinery wasn't limited to his craft; he was also a natural community builder. He co-founded a local woodworking collective, where he brought together artisans, makers, and enthusiasts to share knowledge, resources, and ideas. Through his collective, Collins helped to revitalize the local craft scene, fostering a sense of collaboration and creativity that benefited the entire community.",
